From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:16:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf port: cache the world border

ServerLevel#getWorldBorder looked the border up in the saved data storage (a
hash lookup) on every call, and it is called from the spawn path, entity
ticking and block entity ticking. The border object lives as long as the
level, so keep a reference after the first lookup.

Behaviour: identical (same object, applyInitialSettings is a no-op after the first call).

Ported from Leaf "Cache world border".
Original patch by HaHaWTH <102713261+HaHaWTH@users.noreply.github.com>
Leaf: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf (GPL-3.0-only with section 7(b) attribution term)

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
index ea4cc487002a0edc54cc49bfbecf72be156b6af7..071230501800968cb8326dca78682406173aaadd 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
@@ -200,6 +200,7 @@ public class ServerLevel extends Level implements WorldGenLevel, ServerEntityGet
     private final EntityTickList entityTickList = new EntityTickList();
     private final ServerWaypointManager waypointManager;
     private EnvironmentAttributeSystem environmentAttributes;
+    private @Nullable WorldBorder cachedWorldBorder; // Leaf port - cache world border
     // Paper - rewrite chunk system
     private final GameEventDispatcher gameEventDispatcher;
     public boolean noSave;
@@ -2547,8 +2548,15 @@ public class ServerLevel extends Level implements WorldGenLevel, ServerEntityGet
 
     @Override
     public WorldBorder getWorldBorder() {
+        // Leaf port start - cache world border (Leaf "Cache world border", HaHaWTH)
+        WorldBorder cached = this.cachedWorldBorder;
+        if (cached != null) {
+            return cached;
+        }
+        // Leaf port end - cache world border
         WorldBorder worldBorder = this.getDataStorage().computeIfAbsent(WorldBorder.TYPE);
         worldBorder.applyInitialSettings(this.levelData.getGameTime());
+        this.cachedWorldBorder = worldBorder; // Leaf port - cache world border
         return worldBorder;
     }
 
